>> title: Potato Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: potato, mayonnaise, eggs, side, make-ahead
>> counters: Deli, Meat and Three
>> aka: deli potato salad, american potato salad, creamy potato salad, mustard potato salad, tater salad
>> pairs-with: mayonnaise, coleslaw, sour-dill-pickles
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 50 min
>> slack: forgiving — the vinegar goes onto the potatoes while they are still warm; a cooled potato takes none of it in
>> step.1: boil the potatoes 20 min
>> step.2: cut warm, splash with vinegar, rest 10 min
>> step.3: whisk the dressing
>> step.4: fold in the crunch and the egg
>> step.5: chill 2 hr

Boil @yellow potatoes{3%lb}(1.35 kg, skin on, in even pieces) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @kosher salt{2%Tbs} and ~boil{20%min} from cold, until a knife goes into the middle without the outside falling apart. Waxy potatoes, not russets: a baking potato dissolves into the dressing and turns the whole tub to paste.

Cut @&(~1)drained potatoes{} into rough inch pieces while they are still too hot to hold comfortably, splash @cider vinegar{2%Tbs} over them and ~rest{10%min}. A warm potato drinks vinegar and a cold one wears it — this one step is the difference between potato salad that tastes seasoned through and potato salad that tastes like mayonnaise.

Whisk @mayonnaise{1%cup}(240 mL), @yellow mustard{2%Tbs}, @celery seed{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} smooth.

Fold @&(~1)dressing{} into @&(~2)dressed potatoes{} with @celery{2%ribs}(diced small), @yellow onion{1/2%small}(diced fine), @dill pickle{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @hard-boiled eggs{3}(chopped), keeping the spoon under and over rather than stirring, so the potatoes stay in pieces.

Chill @&(~1)potato salad{} ~chill{2%hr} before serving, and taste it again cold — cold dulls salt, so it will want a little more than it did in the bowl. Dust the top with paprika, which is what the case does, and eat it within three days.
